WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:06.410
House of the Dragon Episode 7 has a funeral
and a wedding....And a dragon flight, and

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.650
a child fight – and a fake murder.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.860
So what happens, and what does it mean?

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.980
This video has no spoilers for Hot D past
Episode 7.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.359
In the previous episode, Laena Velaryon died.

00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:25.050
She was the daughter of Corlys and Rhaenys,
the sister of Laenor, the wife of Daemon,

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.499
and the mother of Baela and Rhaena.

00:00:27.499 --> 00:00:31.509
So the whole royal family comes to her funeral
on Driftmark.

00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:36.170
Many of their dragons also come – the book
says there were so many dragons here, it was

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:38.780
like Driftmark was “the new Valyria”.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:44.510
Valyria was the great dragonlord empire before
its downfall.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:48.039
This dragon appears to be Aegon’s dragon,
Sunfyre.

00:00:48.039 --> 00:00:53.910
The books say Sunfyre is “the most beautiful”,
and “most magnificent dragon ever”, with

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:58.539
“gleaming golden scales and pale pink wing
membranes”.

00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:02.370
And this dragon might be Helaena’s dragon,
Dreamfyre.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:07.440
Dreamfyre is one of the bigger older dragons,
and is coloured “pale blue” with “with

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.960
silvery markings”.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:15.790
So we’ve now seen eight dragons in Hot D.
Luke and Baela also have dragons that we haven’t

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:17.040
seen yet.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.040
Targaryens burn their dead with dragonfire.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:23.170
But the Velaryons historically never had dragons.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:25.710
Their power was ships on the sea.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:29.230
So Laena’s coffin is laid to rest in the
ocean.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:34.160
The showrunner says this ritual is called
“the Seat of the Sea”, and that centuries

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:39.710
of Velaryon sarcophagi form the foundation
of the island of High Tide.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:47.100
Vaemond Velaryon says that the Merling King,
a mermaid god, will guard Laena in the “eternal

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.100
waters”.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:53.030
House Tully’s funeral rites also speak of
an underwater afterlife.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:57.990
And the ironborn believe that after death
they will party with the Drowned God in his

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:01.610
watery halls like a “wet Valhalla”.

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:07.020
In the books, there are hints that the truth
behind these legends of sea gods, is something

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.180
more monstrous and Lovecraftian.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:16.490
But Laena is laid to rest, and her uncle Vaemond
uses his speech to make a political point.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:23.230
Vaemond says that Velaryon blood runs true,
and Velaryon blood “must never thin”.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:28.250
And he looks pointedly at Rhaenyra’s sons
Jace and Luke.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:33.560
Because Jace and Luke are called Velaryon,
but they don’t really have Laenor Velaryon’s

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.550
blood, they’re actually Harwin Strong’s
bastards.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:42.960
Vaemond’s brother Lord Corlys wants Luke
to inherit Driftmark and be the next Velaryon

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:49.250
lord, but Vaemond doesn’t want that – instead
he mentions Laena’s trueborn daughters Baela

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.360
and Rhaena.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:55.880
They have Velaryon blood, so Vaemond seems
to want them to inherit Driftmark.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:03:00.220
We’ve seen Vaemond and Corlys clash before.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:04.510
This could be the beginning of a succession
dispute within House Velaryon.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:10.600
Daemon laughs at Vaemond for using a eulogy
for petty politics.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:16.170
This kind of BS is exactly why Daemon left
court and stayed in Pentos.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:22.540
Corlys tells Luke he’ll inherit Driftmark
– because Jace is heir to the Throne after

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.310
Rhaenyra, and Laenor is king consort.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:29.990
But Luke says he doesn’t want to be lord,
cause that’ll only happen when more of his

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:32.040
family dies.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:38.100
These poor kids are traumatised by all the
death and tragedy around them, but the adults

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:45.690
keep pushing them into politics and conflict
for the sake of their ambitions.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:50.700
Jace knows the truth – he’s not Laenor’s
son, he’s Harwin’s bastard.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:55.760
So Jace says he should get to mourn his father
and grandfather’s death at Harrenhal.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:04:02.030
But Rhaenyra says they both must hide their
grief and pretend that Laenor is Jace’s

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:07.090
father – or else the Velaryons won’t support
them, and as a bastard, Jace’s claim to

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:08.890
the Throne would be weaker.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:13.230
The adults’ political schemes make their
kids suffer.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:19.669
Aemond almost speaks to Jace, but they’re
separated by a fire between them, representing

00:04:19.669 --> 00:04:25.240
their family’s burning conflict, so Aemond
hesitates and backs off.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:30.740
Which is tragic, cause if these boys had talked
and connected, maybe they wouldn’t have

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.719
had that terrible fight later on.

00:04:33.719 --> 00:04:39.340
Helaena Targaryen is the daughter of Viserys
and Alicent, and she likes bugs and saying

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.419
mysterious cryptic hit.

00:04:41.419 --> 00:04:47.550
So Helaena says “Hand turns loom; spool
of green, spool of black; dragons of flesh

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.040
weaving dragons of thread”.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:55.770
The dragons are Targaryens, and the spools
of thread are Viserys’s bloodline.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:59.279
The “spool of green” is Viserys’ children
with Alicent, cause Alicent’s family are

00:04:59.279 --> 00:05:00.279
called the greens.

00:05:00.279 --> 00:05:02.919
The “spool of black” is Rhaenyra and her
kids.

00:05:02.919 --> 00:05:08.449
The hand turning the loom might refer to the
Hand of the King Otto Hightower – cause

00:05:08.449 --> 00:05:14.029
it was Otto’s manipulation that got Alicent
with Viserys and started the spool of green.

00:05:14.029 --> 00:05:18.550
Looms and thread can symbolise fate and destiny.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:24.490
Like the Fates in real mythology who weave
the threads of human destiny on a loom.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:29.280
It seems that Helaena has prophetic dreams
of the future, giving her glimpses of the

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.910
fabric of human destiny.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:36.069
But her visions aren’t very helpful when
no one listens to her.

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:41.050
Helaena is now betrothed to marry her brother
Aegon.

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:46.479
Incest is traditional for the Targaryens – Aegon
the Conqueror married his sisters, King Jaehaerys

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:50.680
married his sister, and Viserys and Daemon’s
parents were siblings.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:56.110
The Targaryens do this to keep their blood
pure, and to keep their dragonriding genes

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.629
in the family.

00:05:57.629 --> 00:06:03.300
Aegon and Helaena’s mother Alicent previously
seemed disgusted by Targaryen incest.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:08.280
She is a religious woman, and the Faith of
the Seven considers incest an abomination

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:13.349
– the Faith tolerates Targaryen incest only
reluctantly.

00:06:13.349 --> 00:06:18.339
So how does Alicent feel her about her children
marrying each other?

00:06:18.339 --> 00:06:22.330
Maybe it was Viserys’ idea, and she just
went along with it.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:27.559
Or maybe Alicent put aside her morality, and
supported this marriage because it’s useful

00:06:27.559 --> 00:06:29.029
politically.

00:06:29.029 --> 00:06:31.879
Alicent wants Aegon to inherit the Throne.

00:06:31.879 --> 00:06:38.210
And marrying his sister makes Aegon seem more
like a legitimate traditional Targaryen king,

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.870
someone who will produce Targaryen dragonriding
heirs.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:46.919
Aegon was probably named Aegon like Aegon
the Conqueror for the same reason, to make

00:06:46.919 --> 00:06:49.550
him seem like a true king.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:55.210
But aside from the name, Alicent’s son is
not much like Aegon the Conqueror.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:58.430
All Aegon wants is to drink and hit on girls.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:05.069
It’s the second son Aemond who is more dutiful,
and more focussed on their family’s strength.

00:07:05.069 --> 00:07:10.099
So Otto Hightower is now Hand of the King
again, to replace Lyonel Strong.

00:07:10.099 --> 00:07:15.449
Previously, Viserys fired Otto because Otto
was manipulative and biased towards his own

00:07:15.449 --> 00:07:16.620
family.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:21.119
But now he’s brought Otto back, maybe under
pressure from Alicent.

00:07:21.119 --> 00:07:25.310
In the books, Viserys considers making Rhaenyra
Hand of the King.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:30.020
But then he doesn’t because that might cause
conflict between Rhaenyra and Alicent.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:34.990
So instead of dealing with this conflict,
Viserys just does the easy thing and lets

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:40.729
Otto have power, despite the fact that Otto
obviously doesn’t support Viserys’ chosen

00:07:40.729 --> 00:07:42.069
heir Rhaenyra.

00:07:42.069 --> 00:07:49.389
The old hatred between Daemon and Otto is
not forgotten – Daemon calls Otto a leech.

00:07:49.389 --> 00:07:55.089
So everyone marinates in their unhappiness,
and glares at each other meaningfully.

00:07:55.089 --> 00:08:01.450
Alicent hates Rhaenyra, Rhaenyra wants Daemon,
Viserys tries to reunite with Daemon, and

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:04.399
Daemon pretends he doesn’t need anyone.

00:08:04.399 --> 00:08:07.869
Viserys mistakenly calls Alicent “Aemma”.

00:08:07.869 --> 00:08:11.229
Aemma was the name of Viserys’ previous
wife.

00:08:11.229 --> 00:08:15.179
It seems like Viserys’ sickness is affecting
his mind.

00:08:15.179 --> 00:08:20.990
Which is scary – if the king loses his marbles,
who will hold this broken family and this

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:22.409
kingdom together?

00:08:22.409 --> 00:08:27.169
It also shows that Aemma is still on Viserys’
mind.

00:08:27.169 --> 00:08:34.120
The actor and writers say that Viserys made
Rhaenyra heir as an act of love for Aemma.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:39.690
Viserys still feels guilty for Aemma’s death
and sees Rhaenyra as the last remnant of the

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:43.130
woman he loved and still loves.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:47.259
Rhaenys and Corlys mourn their dead daughter
Laena.

00:08:47.259 --> 00:08:52.949
Rhaenys says again that Corlys’ political
ambitions put their children in danger.

00:08:52.949 --> 00:08:58.750
To honour Laena, Rhaenys wants Laena’s daughter
Baela to inherit Driftmark – like Vaemond,

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:03.889
she doesn’t support Luke getting Driftmark
because Luke doesn’t have Velaryon blood.

00:09:03.889 --> 00:09:10.649
But Corlys has a different view on legacy
– he says “History does not remember blood.

00:09:10.649 --> 00:09:11.959
It remembers names”.

00:09:11.959 --> 00:09:16.480
Corlys doesn’t care that Luke and Jace aren’t
really his grandkids.

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:21.420
Their names are still Velaryon – while Baela’s
name is Targaryen.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:27.649
Corlys won’t back down on his ambitions,
and Rhaenys is frustrated.

00:09:27.649 --> 00:09:30.440
Rhaenyra reconnects with her uncle Daemon.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:36.819
They talk about their frustrations with their
partners – Daemon didn’t quite love Laena,

00:09:36.819 --> 00:09:39.730
and Rhaenyra says Laenor is “useless”.

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:42.310
Rhaenyra talks about her sexual desires.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:47.800
It was Daemon who awakened Rhaenyra’s desire
– when she was a teenager.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:53.100
Rhaenyra never let go of that attraction,
so she kisses Daemon, and then has sex with

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.670
her uncle on the beach.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:10:03.000
Which is a bad idea for several reasons – like,
they’re outside a funeral, Rhaenyra is married,

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:09.069
and they will get sand in all of their crevices,
but Rhaenyra and Daemon find deep satisfaction

00:10:09.069 --> 00:10:15.940
in putting aside their duties and politics
and lies and just indulging their true desires.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:19.500
Meanwhile, Aemond fulfils his desire.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:26.120
He wants a dragon to fulfil his birthright
as a Targaryen prince, to get power and freedom,

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.700
to stop the other kids bullying him with pigs.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:34.820
In the books, Viserys suggests that Aemond
could claim a dragon egg or a hatchling on

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:36.160
Dragonstone.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:40.279
There are also older dragons like Vermithor
and Silverwing available.

00:10:40.279 --> 00:10:47.339
But Aemond wants nothing less than the biggest
most powerful dragon in the world – Vhagar.

00:10:47.339 --> 00:10:53.110
With her first rider Visenya, Vhagar fought
in Aegon’s Conquest alongside Balerion the

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:55.319
Black Dread and Meraxes.

00:10:55.319 --> 00:10:59.970
She has burned and battled all across Westeros.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:06.149
Most recently, Vhagar was Laena Velaryon’s
dragon, but with Laena dead, Vhagar is available

00:11:06.149 --> 00:11:07.300
again.

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:10.870
So Aemond finds Vhagar sleeping on the beach.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:16.759
According to the Ringer-Verse podcast, a Hot
D sound designer said Vhagar is “old, lonely,

00:11:16.759 --> 00:11:23.100
and has IBS”, and they made a “gigantic”
fart sound for Vhagar which sadly HBO did

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:24.459
not use.

00:11:24.459 --> 00:11:30.190
The books say that Vhagar has become “sleepy”
in her ancient age, and she does not like

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:31.740
being woken up.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:37.740
But Aemond is brave, and as a true Targaryen,
he has the dragonrider blood that makes it

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:44.459
possible to control dragons – it looks like
Vhagar can smell Aemond’s dragon blood.

00:11:44.459 --> 00:11:50.009
Aemond commands Vhagar in Valyrian – he
says “Dohaeras”, meaning serve, and “Lykiri”

00:11:50.009 --> 00:11:51.449
meaning “Be calm”.

00:11:51.449 --> 00:11:56.089
He mounts Vhagar, and says “Soves” meaning
fly.

00:11:56.089 --> 00:12:00.470
And so Aemond rides the greatest dragon through
the sky.

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:05.540
He almost falls off a few times – you are
meant to chain your belt to the saddle so

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:07.160
you don’t fall off.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:12.800
But Aemond survives, proves his manhood, and
bonds with the most powerful weapon of war

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:13.959
in this world.

00:12:13.959 --> 00:12:20.709
Once a rider bonds with a dragon, no one else
can control the dragon until the rider dies.

00:12:20.709 --> 00:12:23.889
So Rhaena and Baela are angry.

00:12:23.889 --> 00:12:28.560
Vhagar was their mother’s dragon, so they
wanted Rhaena to claim Vhagar.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:33.570
There’s no rule that a dragonrider’s child
gets their parent’s dragon.

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:39.290
Like, before Laena, Vhagar’s rider was Baelon
Targaryen, but Baelon’s sons didn’t get

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:41.210
Vhagar, Laena took her.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:47.829
But it’s certainly a faux par to take Vhagar
on the night of Laena’s funeral.

00:12:47.829 --> 00:12:53.060
Baela and Rhaena wake Jace and Luke, and together
they confront Aemond.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:57.690
In the book, Baela and Rhaena aren’t present,
but three-year-old Joffrey Velaryon is there,

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:02.009
and Aemond shoves Joff into a pile of dragon
poop.

00:13:02.009 --> 00:13:09.240
Aemond is full of adrenaline and arrogance,
drunk with new power, so he insults Rhaena,

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:16.200
then Rhaena and Baela attack Aemond, he fights
back, and it turns into an all-out brawl.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:17.550
Which is not surprising.

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:21.940
Cause these boys were trained to fight and
to see each other as enemies.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:27.389
And the adults taught them that bastardy is
a shameful deadly secret.

00:13:27.389 --> 00:13:32.829
So when Aemond calls Jace and Luke “Bastards”
and Strongs, and threatens the brothers, Luke

00:13:32.829 --> 00:13:37.610
slashes Aemond’s face, taking his eye.

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:42.959
In the previous episode, Helaena said that
to get a dragon, Aemond would “have to close

00:13:42.959 --> 00:13:44.360
an eye”.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:48.699
She saw the future, probably in her dreams.

00:13:48.699 --> 00:13:54.690
Aemond later says it’s okay he lost an eye,
because he gained the power of Vhagar.

00:13:54.690 --> 00:14:00.610
In mythology, the sacrifice of an eye can
grant godlike power.

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:04.519
In the aftermath, King Viserys tries to make
peace.

00:14:04.519 --> 00:14:10.589
Alicent sides with Aemond, Rhaenyra sides
with her own sons, and everyone’s pissed.

00:14:10.589 --> 00:14:13.850
Daemon seems to enjoy the conflict and chaos.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:15.510
“It felt like he was happy to watch them
all implode”.

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:16.510
“He's a leaner, Daemon.

00:14:16.510 --> 00:14:21.420
I always liked the idea that he sort of leans”.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:27.680
Jace and Luke say that Aemond called them
bastards, and Rhaenyra says this is high treason,

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:30.509
and “Aemond must be sharply questioned”.

00:14:30.509 --> 00:14:35.689
‘Sharp questioning’ is a euphemism for
torture in interrogation.

00:14:35.689 --> 00:14:42.860
So it’s pretty extreme for Rhaenyra to demand
the torture of an already mutilated child

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:48.449
because that child told the truth about Rhaenyra’s
infidelity, that is.. brazen.

00:14:48.449 --> 00:14:54.449
Rhaenyra brings up these allegations to force
a confrontation, maybe hoping that King Viserys

00:14:54.449 --> 00:14:58.110
will publicly side with her not with Alicent.

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:04.910
Aegon says “Everyone knows” that Jace
and Luke are bastards, just look at them.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:11.879
So the deadly treasonous truth is spoken,
and King Viserys fails to resolve anything.

00:15:11.879 --> 00:15:19.160
He just shouts at everyone in general to just
be cool and be friends please, with his empty

00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:22.579
shirt sleeve flapping impotently.

00:15:22.579 --> 00:15:26.120
Then he tries to leave as though the problem
is solved.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:28.519
But no one is satisfied.

00:15:28.519 --> 00:15:31.019
The king fails to make justice.

00:15:31.019 --> 00:15:38.439
This whole scene is similar to Episode 2 of
Game of Thrones, when Arya Stark fights Joffrey,

00:15:38.439 --> 00:15:42.629
then King Robert fails to make peace.

00:15:42.629 --> 00:15:47.370
The Lannisters and Starks just learn to hate
each other more, and the king’s failure

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:51.259
to make justice plants the seeds for war.

00:15:51.259 --> 00:15:54.499
So Alicent tries to make her own justice.

00:15:54.499 --> 00:16:01.660
She orders Criston to cut out Luke’s eye,
to pay the debt of Aemond’s lost eye.

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:07.930
Criston refuses – he’s not mad enough
to mutilate a prince, but Alicent is.

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:12.309
She takes Viserys’ Valyrian steel knife
and attacks.

00:16:12.309 --> 00:16:18.240
After a lifetime of suppressing her emotions,
of sacrificing her desires for the sake of

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:25.290
others’ expectations, acting courteous and
proper at all times, she finally explodes

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.519
with murderous rage.

00:16:27.519 --> 00:16:33.500
Alicent says that while she’s always done
her duty, Rhaenyra constantly breaks the rules

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:39.540
with her bastards, and lies, flaunting her
freedom with sex and dragonflight.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:45.279
Alicent is bitterly envious that Rhaenyra
gets to do what she wants without consequence,

00:16:45.279 --> 00:16:49.709
and now even escapes justice for the mutilation
of Alicent’s son.

00:16:49.709 --> 00:16:56.730
But Rhaenyra says that Alicent’s righteousness
is a cloak, an excuse – that Alicent acts

00:16:56.730 --> 00:17:03.529
like she’s better than Rhaenyra, but really
she’s just motivated by petty envy and spite.

00:17:03.529 --> 00:17:08.800
The tragedy of this fight is that Rhaenyra
and Alicent were once best friends.

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:13.810
Alicent’s actor said Alicent and Rhaenyra
would've been much stronger together, but

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:19.620
they were driven apart by this political system
– with its restrictions on women’s sexuality,

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:24.750
and on bastards, and its demand for one bloodline
to dominate all others.

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:30.170
It’s cause of the ambitions of men like
Otto, who made Alicent marry Viserys in the

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:37.080
first place – that politics is what drove
Rhaenyra and Alicent apart, that’s why Alicent’s

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:42.310
life sucks, but Alicent projects all her anger
at Rhaenyra.

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:48.020
Rhaenyra is cut with the knife, and their
conflict draws first blood.

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:54.930
The king says he’s done and walks off, leaving
his daughter bleeding at his wife’s hands,

00:17:54.930 --> 00:18:00.180
leaving his son mutilated, leaving his family
divided.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:03.770
The Valyrian steel dagger lies on the floor.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:09.160
This dagger represents the prophecy of Aegon
the Conqueror, the need for House Targaryen

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:13.020
to be united to save the world from the white
walkers.

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:18.440
Viserys fails to uphold this sacred responsibility,.

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:24.470
Rhaenyra stands with Daemon and the Velaryons,
and Alicent with her sons and Criston.

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:29.411
Rhaenyra later calls Alicent’s side “the
greens”, and in the books Rhaenyra’s side

00:18:29.411 --> 00:18:31.320
is called “the blacks”.

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:35.740
Peace between them now seems impossible.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:40.270
Alicent feels guilty and shocked by her violent
outburst.

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:44.290
Rhaenyra said earlier that Alicent isn’t
capable of cold murder.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:48.420
But Daemon replied that everyone is capable
of depravity.

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:54.530
Now, Alicent finds the depravity within herself,
and she’s horrified.

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:57.150
But her father Otto is glad.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:04.400
He’s happy that Alicent has the determination
to win this ugly game, to get Aegon on the

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:06.020
Throne for their house.

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:12.370
He’s also fine with Aemond losing an eye
– it’s worth it to get Vhagar.

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:19.190
So Otto’s family is spiralling into violence,
his daughter assaulting royalty, his grandkid

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:27.030
losing body parts and riding a deadly scaly
nuke, and Otto couldn’t be more proud.

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:32.540
Rhaenyra get stitched up with thread, like
Aemond is stitched up with thread.

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:37.650
This might represent the green and black thread
Helaena mentioned earlier.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:41.560
Laenor Velaryon is having a bad time.

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:45.261
The death of his sister Laena made Laenor
think about his own life.

00:19:45.261 --> 00:19:51.070
And he’s realised that he has failed as
a husband to Rhaenyra, and as an adoptive

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:54.120
father to Jace Luke and Joff.

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:59.280
Rhaenyra mentions that she and Laenor did
try to conceive children together.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:04.530
In the book, Mushroom says that Rhaenyra Laenor
and Qarl had threesomes together.

00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:07.140
But they failed to make a child.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:12.140
It is important that Rhaenyra and Laenor tried
to produce legitimate children.

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:19.010
Cause that means that Rhaenyra was justified
in making kids with someone else – she needs

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:21.950
heirs, and couldn’t get them from Laenor.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:26.900
Though it would’ve been smarter to have
kids with someone who at least looked like

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:31.650
Laenor, rather than with Harwin, whose appearance
makes the bastardy obvious.

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:35.410
Laenor says he wishes he wasn’t born gay.

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:41.470
But Rhaenyra says Laenor’s a good person,
regardless of how society demonises his sexuality.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:47.460
Rhaenyra’s sexuality is scrutinised as well,
and we see how unfair that is when males like

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:50.990
Aegon get to fug around with no consequences.

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:54.130
Laenor takes responsibility for his failures.

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:58.860
He says he’ll stop seeing his boyfriend
Qarl, and will instead dedicate himself to

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.990
Rhaenyra and their family.

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:05.740
He says he’ll sacrifice his happiness for
the sake of his duty.

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:12.740
In Thrones, Aemon says that love is the death
of duty, so Laenor prepares to give up his

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:13.740
love.

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:20.450
Alicent leaves Driftmark, and Corlys and Rhaenys
watch as Vhagar, their daughter’s dragon,

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:26.840
and the greatest weapon in this world, leaves
their control in Aemond’s hands.

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:33.340
Larys Strong slides into Alicent’s DMs and
offers to do a murder – or to get an eyeball

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:35.710
for her, or whatever she wants.

00:21:35.710 --> 00:21:42.600
We know he’s capable of anything, after
he burned his own family with his fireflies.

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:47.880
Maybe Larys wants to please Alicent cause
he’s creepily obsessed with her, or maybe

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:53.820
he wants to make this conflict worse to use
chaos to gain power, or maybe he just loves

00:21:53.820 --> 00:21:54.820
killin’.

00:21:54.820 --> 00:22:01.280
But his offer is like a Faustian pact, a deal
with the devil – he tempts her with power,

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:04.720
but his evil may taint or trap Alicent.

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:11.120
Alicent tells him not to kill anyone – yet
– but that the day will come.

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:16.560
With Larys and Criston and Otto, Alicent is
surrounded by violent men, she’s got three

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:20.140
devils on her shoulder and no angel.

00:22:20.140 --> 00:22:25.510
Rhaenyra tells Daemon that fire cost them
both what they love – cause Rhaenyra’s

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:30.350
lover Harwin and Daemon’s wife Laena both
died in fire.

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:36.160
Fire is destructive, but she says that as
Targaryens, fire is their nature, and they

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:39.070
were made to burn together.

00:22:39.070 --> 00:22:44.350
Rhaenyra proposes marriage to Daemon, both
as a political alliance against Alicent’s

00:22:44.350 --> 00:22:48.270
greens, and as a fulfilment of their true
desires.

00:22:48.270 --> 00:22:52.820
Rhaenyra and Daemon have both had loveless
marriages of duty.

00:22:52.820 --> 00:22:59.770
Now they want a marriage of passion and power,
of fire and blood, of uncle and niece.

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:03.340
But they can’t marry while Rhaenyra is married
to Laenor.

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:07.440
So Rhaenyra and Daemon plan to fake Laenor’s
death.

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:13.110
Daemon gets Laenor’s boyfriend Qarl to stage
a fake fight with Laenor.

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:18.320
Daemon murders some guy, and they burn the
body, so everyone thinks that Qarl killed

00:23:18.320 --> 00:23:20.390
and burned Laenor.

00:23:20.390 --> 00:23:25.080
Rhaenyra wants people to think that she paid
Qarl to kill Laenor.

00:23:25.080 --> 00:23:29.850
She wants people to think she’s a killer,
so that as a ruler, she’ll be feared.

00:23:29.850 --> 00:23:35.080
She doesn’t want to be disrespected as a
weak ruler like her father Viserys is.

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:41.160
But the truth is that Rhaenyra loves Laenor,
she appreciates his devotion earlier, so she

00:23:41.160 --> 00:23:45.740
sets him free, lets him choose love over duty.

00:23:45.740 --> 00:23:49.240
So Laenor rows into the sunset with Qarl.

00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:55.710
Laenor shaves his head to hide his Velaryon
identity, to free himself from the restrictions

00:23:55.710 --> 00:23:57.590
of his responsibilities.

00:23:57.590 --> 00:24:03.780
Laenor leaves his family, and his dragon Seasmoke,
which would be hard.

00:24:03.780 --> 00:24:09.770
Laenor loves Seasmoke – can a dragonrider
ever really separate from their dragon?

00:24:09.770 --> 00:24:14.970
In Game of Thrones, Daenerys tries to separate
from her dragons, but that doesn’t last.

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:18.510
The dragonrider bond is deep – and magic.

00:24:18.510 --> 00:24:23.830
There are hints in the books that dragons
can sense their riders’ location – so

00:24:23.830 --> 00:24:26.910
maybe Seasmoke will try to find Laenor.

00:24:26.910 --> 00:24:30.250
But that would reveal to everyone that Laenor’s
still alive.

00:24:30.250 --> 00:24:36.870
Also, as long as Laenor is alive it may be
impossible for anyone new to bond with Seasmoke,

00:24:36.870 --> 00:24:40.110
and that could give away that Laenor’s alive.

00:24:40.110 --> 00:24:45.860
So as a Valyrian dragonrider, can Laenor really
escape his destiny?

00:24:45.860 --> 00:24:48.760
When Daemon went east, he couldn’t stay
away.

00:24:48.760 --> 00:24:51.440
Laenor’s escape is a change from the books.

00:24:51.440 --> 00:24:56.710
In the books it seems that Laenor really is
killed by Qarl – but Fire &amp; Blood is all

00:24:56.710 --> 00:25:02.360
about unreliable narrators, and historians
not knowing the full truth.

00:25:02.360 --> 00:25:08.160
So Hot D can give us these twists to surprise
even people who’ve read the books.

00:25:08.160 --> 00:25:13.960
With Laenor gone, Rhaenyra and Daemon get
married in an ancient Valyrian ritual.

00:25:13.960 --> 00:25:18.800
Maybe Daemon learned about this from those
Valyrian books in Pentos.

00:25:18.800 --> 00:25:23.190
All Valyrian sorcery is rooted in blood or
fire.

00:25:23.190 --> 00:25:29.550
So they’re surrounded by candles, and wear
fiery clothes, and they draw blood with dragonglass

00:25:29.550 --> 00:25:35.350
– the special volcanic rock found on Dragonstone
that can kill white walkers.

00:25:35.350 --> 00:25:40.980
They draw Valyrian glyphs on each other that
mean fire and blood.

00:25:40.980 --> 00:25:45.680
So this wedding is not like Rhaenyra and Daemon’s
previous marriages.

00:25:45.680 --> 00:25:53.270
This one is passionate and grand, with the
weight and possibly the magic of ancient ceremony.

00:25:53.270 --> 00:25:57.860
Rhaenyra says this marriage strengthens Rhaenyra’s
claim to the Throne.

00:25:57.860 --> 00:26:02.090
Because it combines Rhaenyra’s claim as
Viserys’ daughter with Dameon’s claim

00:26:02.090 --> 00:26:03.770
as Viserys’ brother.

00:26:03.770 --> 00:26:07.570
But this also might turn people against Rhaenyra.

00:26:07.570 --> 00:26:12.440
Some people don’t want Daemon anywhere near
the Throne, because he’s so violent and

00:26:12.440 --> 00:26:13.440
unpredictable.

00:26:13.440 --> 00:26:19.780
And it may be seen as an insult that Rhaenyra
and Daemon remarried so soon after Laena and

00:26:19.780 --> 00:26:21.790
Laenor’s apparent deaths.

00:26:21.790 --> 00:26:27.030
King Viserys will be pissed, because this
royal marriage happened without his permission.

00:26:27.030 --> 00:26:32.580
And the apparent death of Laenor could weaken
Rhaenyra’s alliance with the Velaryons.

00:26:32.580 --> 00:26:38.370
Will the Corlys and Rhaenys think that Rhaenyra
killed their son, or will Rhaenyra tell them

00:26:38.370 --> 00:26:40.850
the truth?

00:26:40.850 --> 00:26:44.550
Like fire, this marriage is powerful but dangerous.

00:26:44.550 --> 00:26:49.380
Rhaenyra’s actor says Rhaenyra and Daemon
are “a terrible match” because they’re

00:26:49.380 --> 00:26:53.350
so similar, they are have a “dangerous chemistry”.

00:26:53.350 --> 00:26:56.360
Rhaenyra has wanted this marriage for a long
time.

00:26:56.360 --> 00:26:58.920
But will Daemon be a good husband?

00:26:58.920 --> 00:27:02.150
He doesn’t have a great track record.

00:27:02.150 --> 00:27:08.490
So as divisions deepen between Alicent’s
greens and Rhaenyra’s blacks, both sides

00:27:08.490 --> 00:27:12.150
turn to their darkest most dangerous allies.

00:27:12.150 --> 00:27:17.650
The whole royal family spirals towards blood
and fire.

00:27:17.650 --> 00:27:22.470
If you wanna know the full story of the Targaryens,
you’ve gotta check out the Game of Thrones

00:27:22.470 --> 00:27:28.370
books – there’s the main series, the worldbook,
Dunk &amp; Egg, and Fire &amp; Blood, which tells

00:27:28.370 --> 00:27:30.520
the story of Hot D is in Fire &amp; Blood.

